  <div class="section-content">
    <h2>Conceptual framework of the research study</h2>
    <p>The theoretical model of this research study is shown in Figure 4, which depicts the linkages between social media platforms, the selected dimensions, benefits and influence on the intention to recommend the use of social media to others. It also shows the relationships between various dimensions and its outcome in terms of benefits and its impact on the intention to recommend to the use of social media.</p>
    <p>The model has covered three dimensions viz., technological aspects, the component of socialization and issues being faced by users of social media.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-content">
    <h2>Figure 3: Model of Satisfaction and Intention for Social Media</h2>
    <div class="table-container">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Social Media Community</th>
            <th>Outcome</th>
            <th>Social Media Corporates</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Ease of Use</td>
            <td>Satisfaction</td>
            <td>HAPPENED IN PAST</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Usefulness</td>
            <td>Usage Intention of Social Media</td>
            <td>HAPPENING CURRENTLY</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Security</td>
            <td></td>
            <td>TO HAPPEN IN FUTURE</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Involvement</td>
            <td></td>
            <td></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="figure-caption">Figure 3: Model of Satisfaction and Intention for Social Media</p>
      <p class="figure-caption">Source: Jean-Su Lim et al. (2013) and contentmarketinginstitute.com.</p>
    </div>
    <p>The model displayed in Figure 3 is an all-encompassing model, which reveals the linkages between social media usage by the community, corporate entities and its outcome in terms of satisfaction from social media and strengthening the intention to use social media. The components of social media community engagement viz., ease of use, usefulness, security, and involvement, which constitutes into satisfaction from social media results in usage intention of social media.</p>
    <p>The corporate sector also actively engages in brand building to enhance visibility keeping in mind past achievements, present conditions and future aspirations related to social media. Social media platforms stimulate collaboration. The plethora of communication platforms available today are enhanced and evolving in the practices followed to manage marketing, administration and other aspects of the business as they venture to grab the attention of today's empowered consumers. The point of worry is phishing, cyber-attacks, bullying and privacy (Jean-Su Lim et al., 2013; and contentmarketinginstitute.com).</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-content">
    <h2>Figure 4: Conceptual Framework of Use of Social Media</h2>
    <div class="table-container">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>SELECTED TECHNOLOGY ASPECTS</th>
            <th>SOCIALIZATION</th>
            <th>SOCIAL MEDIA IS BENEFICIAL</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>[Accessibility of the Internet, Use of Mobile Phone, Linking of Social Media with Aadhaar Card, Reading of Blogs, YouTube, Slide Share, Development of Social Network, Instant Messaging, Link with other websites]</td>
            <td>[Presence of Popular Persons, Shopping, Social Networking, Information Sharing, Creating, Strengthening Interpersonal Relationships, Connecting with friends and family, Sharing life events, Opinions on current social events, Influence on Relationships]</td>
            <td>[Intention to Use Social Media]</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td></td>
            <td>ISSUES</td>
            <td>RECOMMENDATION OF USE OF SOCIAL MEDIA TO OTHERS</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td></td>
            <td>[Experienced Fraud, Hacking of Social Media Accounts, Fake News, Privacy Issues, Cyberbullying, Cyber Warfare, etc.]</td>
            <td></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="figure-caption">Figure 4: Conceptual Framework of Use of Social Media</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-content">
    <p>The use of technology component includes accessibility to the internet, use of mobile phones, linking of social media with Aadhaar card, reading of blogs, YouTube, Slide Share, development of social network, instant messaging, and link with other websites. The socialization component includes viz., presence of popular persons, shopping, decisions, live-in relationships, creating, strengthening interpersonal relationships, connecting with friends and family, sharing life events, opinions on current social events, and influence on relationships.</p>
    <p>The issues faced by users of social media include experiencing fraudulent hacking of social media account, fake news, immediate sharing, content and share, lack of control on content shared, addiction, exact information not available, feeling of stress, and cyberbullying. These issues are detrimental to the users and the society.</p>
  </div>

